WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:04.658
- It's like drinking lemon juice.

00:00:04.658 --> 00:00:07.158
(sighs) Okay.

00:00:12.646 --> 00:00:14.799
Hi, I'm Hannah, your friendly
neighborhood Wine Mom,

00:00:14.799 --> 00:00:16.522
and I'm drinking some

00:00:16.522 --> 00:00:18.987
really, really sour sauv blanc tonight.

00:00:18.987 --> 00:00:21.308
It's just like the fridge
leftovers, you know,

00:00:21.308 --> 00:00:23.379
when you have the wine that's
been in your fridge for awhile

00:00:23.379 --> 00:00:25.048
that someone brought to
your house and you're like,

00:00:25.048 --> 00:00:26.676
"Oh, I don't really like this kind."

00:00:26.676 --> 00:00:28.480
But, like, I'm not gonna waste.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.420
My phone is shattered to oblivion

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.082
and every time that I text somebody,

00:00:32.082 --> 00:00:34.182
I get shards of glass
in my fingers right now.

00:00:34.182 --> 00:00:35.483
So tonight we're gonna talk about

00:00:35.483 --> 00:00:37.092
the worst things about texting.

00:00:37.092 --> 00:00:39.211
So first, when I text someone,

00:00:39.211 --> 00:00:41.960
and I see the little
bubble appear in the text,

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.227
and then it disappears.

00:00:43.227 --> 00:00:45.142
It's like emotional torture,

00:00:45.142 --> 00:00:47.228
'cause I'm sitting here like (gasps)

00:00:47.228 --> 00:00:48.061
(sighs)

00:00:48.061 --> 00:00:48.894
(gasps)

00:00:48.894 --> 00:00:49.827
(sighs)

00:00:49.827 --> 00:00:51.083
Why would you do that to me?

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:52.896
'Cause it's always in response to a text

00:00:52.896 --> 00:00:57.108
that's either emotional or time-sensitive.

00:00:57.108 --> 00:01:01.086
I've tried to comprehend what
kind of situation could occur

00:01:01.086 --> 00:01:04.056
where you start typing a
text and then you stop.

00:01:04.056 --> 00:01:05.971
And the only explanation I could think of

00:01:05.971 --> 00:01:08.969
is you were standing atop a volcano

00:01:08.969 --> 00:01:10.359
and you're trying to take
a really great picture

00:01:10.359 --> 00:01:13.609
of the center of the volcano
and then you drop your phone.

00:01:13.609 --> 00:01:16.629
Whenever I text my husband
something very, very important,

00:01:16.629 --> 00:01:19.251
like, "Do you want pizza
for dinner tonight?"

00:01:19.251 --> 00:01:21.757
And he types something
and then I never get it.

00:01:21.757 --> 00:01:22.736
Oh, you didn't text me back?

00:01:22.736 --> 00:01:23.569
Guess what?

00:01:23.569 --> 00:01:25.637
We're having tuna noodle
casserole for dinner tonight.

00:01:25.637 --> 00:01:27.693
I suck at making tuna noodle casserole.

00:01:27.693 --> 00:01:28.555
You could've been having

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:31.379
delicious cheesy grease bread with me,

00:01:31.379 --> 00:01:33.279
but you couldn't text me back.

00:01:33.279 --> 00:01:36.559
Next, the entire etiquette
of dating and texting.

00:01:36.559 --> 00:01:39.068
Now, I haven't dated in a very long time,

00:01:39.068 --> 00:01:40.735
but when I did date,

00:01:41.607 --> 00:01:42.979
there was this weird time period

00:01:42.979 --> 00:01:45.104
that you're supposed to wait
before you text somebody back.

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:47.069
It's like two hours is acceptable,

00:01:47.069 --> 00:01:49.503
because you seem busy and unavailable.

00:01:49.503 --> 00:01:52.060
I don't want someone
who's too busy for me.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:54.279
I want someone who's interested in me.

00:01:54.279 --> 00:01:56.562
So if I'm free, I will text you back.

00:01:56.562 --> 00:01:58.903
If I'm interested in you,
I will text you back.

00:01:58.903 --> 00:02:01.672
If I'm busy, I will text
you back when I'm free.

00:02:01.672 --> 00:02:04.016
And it's not this, "Oh,
I better seem busy,

00:02:04.016 --> 00:02:05.937
"because then he'll like me more."

00:02:05.937 --> 00:02:08.937
When I'd be dating a guy and
text him and he wouldn't answer

00:02:08.937 --> 00:02:10.380
for a couple hours, I'd be like,

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:11.358
"I know that you're sitting on your bed

00:02:11.358 --> 00:02:13.414
"with no pants, eating a cheeseburger."

00:02:13.414 --> 00:02:15.023
You are not too busy to text me back.

00:02:15.023 --> 00:02:18.469
This too busy to text
persona is not attractive.

00:02:18.469 --> 00:02:21.661
And that's why I married
a phone call kinda guy.

00:02:21.661 --> 00:02:23.844
My husband likes to call people.

00:02:23.844 --> 00:02:25.050
And that's why I love him.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:26.068
So cheers.

00:02:26.068 --> 00:02:27.877
Next, when someone sends me a text

00:02:27.877 --> 00:02:30.909
and then immediately calls me
to ask if I got their text.

00:02:30.909 --> 00:02:34.233
First, you didn't even give
me a chance to open your text.

00:02:34.233 --> 00:02:38.596
Second, if what you had to say
was all wrapped up in a text,

00:02:38.596 --> 00:02:41.732
why are you calling me to
tell me the same exact thing?

00:02:41.732 --> 00:02:43.710
And my mom is one of the
worst offenders of this,

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:45.032
because she will send me a text,

00:02:45.032 --> 00:02:46.503
it's like a picture of
a dress, being like,

00:02:46.503 --> 00:02:47.482
"Do you like this dress?"

00:02:47.482 --> 00:02:49.533
And then she'll call me
literally two seconds later,

00:02:49.533 --> 00:02:50.927
being like, "Did you get my text?"

00:02:50.927 --> 00:02:53.613
And sometimes the text
has not even gone through!

00:02:53.613 --> 00:02:54.930
So then I have to be on the phone like,

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:57.751
"Okay, let me put you on
speaker, let me check my texts.

00:02:57.751 --> 00:02:59.913
"No, it still hasn't, okay
now it's gone through,

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:02.652
"Now I'll look at the picture,
yeah I like the dress."

00:03:02.652 --> 00:03:05.738
Next, when I get a text that
says, "Can we talk later?"

00:03:05.738 --> 00:03:07.181
And it makes me so nervous!

00:03:07.181 --> 00:03:09.098
'Cause I'm like, what is it,
do you not wanna be my friend?

00:03:09.098 --> 00:03:10.325
Did I do something wrong?

00:03:10.325 --> 00:03:11.158
What did I do?

00:03:11.158 --> 00:03:13.049
I retraced my steps for
the last four months.

00:03:13.049 --> 00:03:14.365
What did I do in the last four months?

00:03:14.365 --> 00:03:15.515
Could I have pissed you off somehow?

00:03:15.515 --> 00:03:16.348
What is happening?

00:03:16.348 --> 00:03:18.200
So you're basically
sending me a text saying,

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.888
"Hey, I want you to worry
until the time that we can

00:03:20.888 --> 00:03:22.063
"actually talk."

00:03:22.063 --> 00:03:24.298
If you send something back saying, "What?"

00:03:24.298 --> 00:03:26.142
They're like, "Oh, no,
we'll talk about it later."

00:03:26.142 --> 00:03:28.164
In the time between when
you send me that text

00:03:28.164 --> 00:03:29.428
and we actually talk,

00:03:29.428 --> 00:03:32.148
I've formulated 80,000
different things that lead to

00:03:32.148 --> 00:03:33.714
the world ending.

00:03:33.714 --> 00:03:35.762
And then when it gets to the
time that we actually talk,

00:03:35.762 --> 00:03:36.780
it's always something like,

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:39.613
"Hey, do you like my new haircut?"

00:03:42.129 --> 00:03:44.449
Next, when I get a text and I read it

00:03:44.449 --> 00:03:46.050
and I'm in the middle of something else,

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:48.527
and then I forget to answer
it for like two weeks.

00:03:48.527 --> 00:03:50.498
This happens to me all
the time when I'm at work,

00:03:50.498 --> 00:03:52.151
I'll be in the middle of a shoot

00:03:52.151 --> 00:03:54.066
or I'll be in the middle
of a conference call

00:03:54.066 --> 00:03:54.899
and someone'll text me saying,

00:03:54.899 --> 00:03:57.077
"Hey, do you think I should
wear this shirt or this shirt

00:03:57.077 --> 00:03:58.112
"to my date tonight?"

00:03:58.112 --> 00:04:00.350
And I read it and I'm like,
"Oh yeah, I like that shirt,"

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:01.433
and set it down.

00:04:01.433 --> 00:04:03.546
And I forget for like two weeks.

00:04:03.546 --> 00:04:07.405
I'm a mother of two, I have
a husband who's very needy.

00:04:07.405 --> 00:04:08.671
I work full-time.

00:04:08.671 --> 00:04:10.263
I have a million responsibilities,

00:04:10.263 --> 00:04:12.506
and it's really hard for me to remember

00:04:12.506 --> 00:04:14.737
to reply to a text when
I've read it and already

00:04:14.737 --> 00:04:16.385
like, closed it out and put my phone down.

00:04:16.385 --> 00:04:17.350
Then it's kind of just, like,

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:18.521
out of sight, out of mind.

00:04:18.521 --> 00:04:20.771
So then I'm the jerk who
two weeks later is like,

00:04:20.771 --> 00:04:22.510
"I like the red top!"

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:24.006
I will take full responsibility,

00:04:24.006 --> 00:04:25.529
I am so sorry!

00:04:25.529 --> 00:04:29.228
I am a contributor to one of
the worst things about texting.

00:04:29.228 --> 00:04:31.421
And last, group texts.

00:04:31.421 --> 00:04:33.951
I have gotten group texts to me

00:04:33.951 --> 00:04:36.937
and 10 other people at a
time, and it'll be like,

00:04:36.937 --> 00:04:38.182
"Hey, just want you to know

00:04:38.182 --> 00:04:39.834
"that my birthday party's this Saturday,"

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:43.232
something you could easily
text all 10 of us individually,

00:04:43.232 --> 00:04:45.451
but no, you had to do it as a group text.

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:48.311
So then all 10 of those
people have to be like,

00:04:48.311 --> 00:04:49.737
"Oh my gosh, how's your boyfriend?

00:04:49.737 --> 00:04:50.620
"How's your life?

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:51.498
"How's your job?

00:04:51.498 --> 00:04:52.331
"What's going on?"

00:04:52.331 --> 00:04:54.453
All these individual conversations

00:04:54.453 --> 00:04:56.655
appear within the group text.

00:04:56.655 --> 00:05:00.323
And so I go to my phone and
I have like 87 notifications

00:05:00.323 --> 00:05:02.992
of text messages, none
of which are for me.

00:05:02.992 --> 00:05:05.798
'Cause when I delete the
message conversation,

00:05:05.798 --> 00:05:08.518
I still get notified the next
time someone sends a message.

00:05:08.518 --> 00:05:10.700
It doesn't take me out
of the conversation.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.282
And it's so frustrating.

00:05:12.282 --> 00:05:13.426
So the only way to get out of it

00:05:13.426 --> 00:05:14.739
is to be that jerk who's like,

00:05:14.739 --> 00:05:16.278
"Hey guys, can you take this to your own

00:05:16.278 --> 00:05:17.687
"private text conversations?

00:05:17.687 --> 00:05:19.581
"Because this has nothing to do with me."

00:05:19.581 --> 00:05:22.015
That's all I had to say.

00:05:22.015 --> 00:05:22.848
So that's all I've got for today.

00:05:22.848 --> 00:05:24.744
I'm Hannah, your friendly
neighborhood Wine Mom,

00:05:24.744 --> 00:05:26.990
and if you have any problems with texting

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:27.889
that you wanna talk about,

00:05:27.889 --> 00:05:31.054
or a topic you want me to talk
about in a future episode,

00:05:31.054 --> 00:05:33.005
leave it in the comments,

00:05:33.005 --> 00:05:34.248
or text me!

00:05:34.248 --> 00:05:35.446
And this is a real phone number,

00:05:35.446 --> 00:05:37.401
and if you're very lucky,
I might text you back!

00:05:37.401 --> 00:05:39.156
'Till next time!

00:05:39.156 --> 00:05:43.045
Oh my god, get me off this group text!

00:05:43.045 --> 00:05:45.957
(groans)

00:05:45.957 --> 00:05:47.040
I don't care.

